<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Humanitarian hydration principles"><div><strong>Safe water comes first</strong><span>Any powdered hydration product depends on safe preparation water and hygienic handling.</span></div><div><strong>Use the right ORS</strong><span>Diarrhoeal dehydration requires appropriately formulated oral rehydration solution and clinical escalation when severe.</span></div><div><strong>Design for the system</strong><span>Cost, packaging, climate, supply chain, local training and waste all affect whether an intervention works at scale.</span></div></div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">ORS for a brighter tomorrow</p><h2>Use the right solution for the problem</h2><p>World Health Organization reduced-osmolarity oral rehydration salts are a defined therapeutic formulation for diarrhoeal dehydration. The current Best Hydrate consumer product is not represented as equivalent to therapeutic ORS.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Field pilot · Botswana · May 2026</p><h2>A first field-learning step</h2><p>In May 2026, Best Hydrate completed a small community distribution pilot in Botswana, coordinated locally by Oratile in Gaborone and the Goodhope area. Product and printed preparation guidance were delivered to community recipients.</p><p>The pilot helped us learn about local coordination, transport, instructions and last-mile delivery. <strong>It was not a clinical study and no treatment or health outcomes were measured.</strong></p><p><em>Thank you to Oratile for helping coordinate the effort.</em></p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Field principle</span><h3>Start small. Learn locally.</h3><p>Build future programs around local partners, appropriate formulation and transparent evidence.</p></aside></section>

